{"id":"mahabharata-7-013","work":"mahabharata","part":7,"partName":"द्रोणपर्व","partNameEn":"Drona Parva","unit":13,"title":"त्रयोदशोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 13 · Drona's mighty fight","summary":{"en":"Drona rampages like fire through the Pandava lines while the rakshasas Ghatotkacha and Alambusha fight each other. Abhimanyu attacks the Kaurava chiefs, and Drona's forces shatter many Pandava divisions.","kn":"ದ್ರೋಣ ಬೆಂಕಿಯಂತೆ ಪಾಂಡವ ಸಾಲುಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ಹರಿದಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ; ರಾಕ್ಷಸರಾದ ಘಟೋತ್ಕಚ-ಅಲಂಬುಷರು ಪರಸ್ಪರ ಹೋರಾಡುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಅಭಿಮನ್ಯು ಕೌರವ ಮುಖ್ಯರ ಮೇಲೆ ದಾಳಿ ಮಾಡುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"द्रोण अग्नि की तरह पाण्डव पंक्तियों में फैलते हैं, राक्षस घटोत्कच और अलम्बुष एक-दूसरे से लड़ते हैं। अभिमन्यु कौरव प्रमुखों पर आक्रमण करता है।","te":"ద్రోణుడు అగ్నిలా పాండవ వరుసల్లో చెలరేగుతాడు; రాక్షసులు ఘటోత్కచ, అలంబుషులు ఒకరితో ఒకరు పోరాడతారు. అభిమన్యుడు కౌరవ ముఖ్యులపై దాడి చేస్తాడు.","ta":"த்ரோணர் நெருப்பு போல் பாண்டவ அணிகளில் பாய்கிறார்; அரக்கர்களான கடோத்கசனும் அலம்புசனும் ஒருவரோடு ஒருவர் போரிடுகின்றனர். அபிமன்யு கௌரவத் தலைவர்களைத் தாக்குகிறான்.","ml":"ദ്രോണർ തീപോലെ പാണ്ഡവ നിരകളിൽ വിഹരിക്കുന്നു; രാക്ഷസരായ ഘടോൽക്കചനും അലംബുഷനും തമ്മിൽ പോരടിക്കുന്നു. അഭിമന്യു കൗരവ നേതാക്കളെ ആക്രമിക്കുന്നു; ദ്രോണരുടെ സൈന്യം നിരവധി പാണ്ഡവ വിഭാഗങ്ങളെ തകർക്കുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 7.13; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Tue Sep 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"द्रोणाभिषेकपर्व","titleEn":"Dronabhisheka Parva (Drona's consecration)","verses":[{"text":"संजय उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Sanjaya said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततः स पाण्डवानीके जनयंस्तुमुलं महत् ।\nव्यचरत्पाण्डवान्द्रोणो दहन्कक्षमिवानलः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, raising a great tumult in the Pandava army, Drona roamed among the Pandavas like fire burning dry grass."}},{"n":2,"text":"निर्दहन्तमनीकानि साक्षादग्निमिवोत्थितम् ।\nदृष्ट्वा रुक्मरथं युद्धे समकम्पन्त सृञ्जयाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the man of the golden chariot burning the divisions in battle like fire itself risen up, the Srinjayas trembled."}},{"n":3,"text":"प्रततं चास्यमानस्य धनुषोऽस्याशुकारिणः ।\nज्याघोषः श्रूयतेऽत्यर्थं विस्फूर्जितमिवाशनेः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As that quick-handed man kept shooting his stretched bow, the twang of the string was heard loudly, like the crash of thunder."}},{"n":4,"text":"रथिनः सादिनश्चैव नागानश्वान्पदातिनः ।\nरौद्रा हस्तवता मुक्ताः प्रमथ्नन्ति स्म सायकाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Loosed by his skilled hand, the terrible arrows crushed chariot-warriors, horsemen, elephants, horses and footmen."}},{"n":5,"text":"नानद्यमानः पर्जन्यः सानिलः शुचिसंक्षये ।\nअश्मवर्षमिवावर्षत्परेषामावहद्भयम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Like a rain cloud with wind at the end of summer, roaring, he rained something like hail and brought fear to the enemy."}},{"n":6,"text":"व्यचरत्स तदा राजन्सेनां विक्षोभयन्प्रभुः ।\nवर्धयामास संत्रासं शात्रवाणाममानुषम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The lord then moved about, stirring up the army and increasing the superhuman terror of his foes."}},{"n":7,"text":"तस्य विद्युदिवाभ्रेषु चापं हेमपरिष्कृतम् ।\nभ्रमद्रथाम्बुदे तस्मिन्दृश्यते स्म पुनः पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"His gold-adorned bow was seen again and again like lightning in the clouds, in that cloud of his whirling chariot."}},{"n":8,"text":"स वीरः सत्यवान्प्राज्ञो धर्मनित्यः सुदारुणः ।\nयुगान्तकाले यन्तेव रौद्रां प्रास्कन्दयन्नदीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That hero, truthful, wise, ever righteous yet most terrible, like a driver at the end of the age, set a terrible river flowing."}},{"n":9,"text":"अमर्षवेगप्रभवां क्रव्यादगणसंकुलाम् ।\nबलौघैः सर्वतः पूर्णां वीरवृक्षापहारिणीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was born of the force of rage, thronged with flocks of flesh-eaters, full on every side of floods of troops, sweeping away the trees that were heroes."}},{"n":10,"text":"शोणितोदां रथावर्तां हस्त्यश्वकृतरोधसम् ।\nकवचोडुपसंयुक्तां मांसपङ्कसमाकुलाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Its water was blood, its whirlpools chariots, its banks made of elephants and horses, with armor for its rafts, and mired with flesh."}},{"n":11,"text":"मेदोमज्जास्थिसिकतामुष्णीषवरफेनिलाम् ।\nसंग्रामजलदापूर्णां प्रासमत्स्यसमाकुलाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Its sand was fat, marrow and bone, its fine foam turbans, full of the water-clouds of battle, thronged with spears for fish."}},{"n":12,"text":"नरनागाश्वसंभूतां शरवेगौघवाहिनीम् ।\nशरीरदारुशृङ्गाटां भुजनागसमाकुलाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It arose from men, elephants and horses, flowing with the force of the flood of arrows, with bodies as logs and crossings, and arms as serpents."}},{"n":13,"text":"उत्तमाङ्गोपलतलां निस्त्रिंशझषसेविताम् ।\nरथनागह्रदोपेतां नानाभरणनीरजाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Its stones were heads, it was frequented by swords for fish, with chariots and elephants as pools and various ornaments as lotuses."}},{"n":14,"text":"महारथशतावर्तां भूमिरेणूर्मिमालिनीम् ।\nमहावीर्यवतां संख्ये सुतरां भीरुदुस्तराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It had hundreds of great chariot-warriors as whirlpools and dust of the earth as waves, easy to cross for the great heroes in battle and hard to cross for the timid."}},{"n":15,"text":"शूरव्यालसमाकीर्णां प्राणिवाणिजसेविताम् ।\nछिन्नच्छत्रमहाहंसां मुकुटाण्डजसंकुलाम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was strewn with heroes as snakes, frequented by the merchants of life, with cut umbrellas as great swans and crowns as birds' eggs."}},{"n":16,"text":"चक्रकूर्मां गदानक्रां शरक्षुद्रझषाकुलाम् ।\nबडगृध्रसृगालानां घोरसंघैर्निषेविताम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Its turtles were wheels, its crocodiles maces, its small fish arrows, and it was frequented by terrible flocks of herons, vultures and jackals."}},{"n":17,"text":"निहतान्प्राणिनः संख्ये द्रोणेन बलिना शरैः ।\nवहन्तीं पितृलोकाय शतशो राजसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"It bore beings killed in battle by mighty Drona's arrows, hundreds of them, O best of kings, toward the world of the ancestors."}},{"n":18,"text":"शरीरशतसंबाधां केशशैवलशाद्वलाम् ।\nनदीं प्रावर्तयद्राजन्भीरूणां भयवर्धिनीम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Crowded with hundreds of bodies, with hair for moss and grass, that river, O king, increased the fear of the timid."}},{"n":19,"text":"तं जयन्तमनीकानि तानि तान्येव भारत ।\nसर्वतोऽभ्यद्रवन्द्रोणं युधिष्ठिरपुरोगमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As he went conquering, those divisions with Yudhishthira in front rushed at Drona from every side, O Bharata."}},{"n":20,"text":"तानभिद्रवतः शूरांस्तावका दृढकार्मुकाः ।\nसर्वतः प्रत्यगृह्णन्त तदभूल्लोमहर्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the heroes charged, your men with firm bows received them on every side, and it was hair-raising."}},{"n":21,"text":"शतमायस्तु शकुनिः सहदेवं समाद्रवत् ।\nसनियन्तृध्वजरथं विव्याध निशितैः शरैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shakuni, of a hundred tricks, rushed at Sahadeva, and pierced him, with his charioteer, banner and chariot, with sharp arrows."}},{"n":22,"text":"तस्य माद्रीसुतः केतुं धनुः सूतं हयानपि ।\nनातिक्रुद्धः शरैश्छित्त्वा षष्ट्या विव्याध मातुलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The son of Madri, not greatly angry, cut down his banner, bow, charioteer and horses with arrows, and pierced his maternal uncle with sixty."}},{"n":23,"text":"सौबलस्तु गदां गृह्य प्रचस्कन्द रथोत्तमात् ।\nस तस्य गदया राजन्रथात्सूतमपातयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Subala's son, taking up a mace, leapt from his fine chariot, and with the mace struck the charioteer of the other off his chariot, O king."}},{"n":24,"text":"ततस्तौ विरथौ राजन्गदाहस्तौ महाबलौ ।\nचिक्रीडतू रणे शूरौ सशृङ्गाविव पर्वतौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the two mighty heroes, both without chariots and mace in hand, played in the battle like two horned mountains, O king."}},{"n":25,"text":"द्रोणः पाञ्चालराजानं विद्ध्वा दशभिराशुगैः ।\nबहुभिस्तेन चाभ्यस्तस्तं विव्याध शताधिकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Drona pierced the king of the Panchalas with ten swift arrows, and he, pierced many times in return, pierced Drona with more than a hundred."}},{"n":26,"text":"विविंशतिं भीमसेनो विंशत्या निशितैः शरैः ।\nविद्ध्वा नाकम्पयद्वीरस्तदद्भुतमिवाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhimasena pierced Vivimshati with twenty sharp arrows but did not shake him, and that was a marvel."}},{"n":27,"text":"विविंशतिस्तु सहसा व्यश्वकेतुशरासनम् ।\nभीमं चक्रे महाराज ततः सैन्यान्यपूजयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Vivimshati suddenly made Bhima horseless, bannerless and bowless, O great king, and the armies praised him."}},{"n":28,"text":"स तन्न ममृषे वीरः शत्रोर्विजयमाहवे ।\nततोऽस्य गदया दान्तान्हयान्सर्वानपातयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The hero could not bear the enemy's victory in the fight, and with his mace he felled all of the other's trained horses."}},{"n":29,"text":"शल्यस्तु नकुलं वीरः स्वस्रीयं प्रियमात्मनः ।\nविव्याध प्रहसन्बाणैर्लाडयन्कोपयन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shalya, the hero, laughing, pierced with arrows Nakula, his dear sister's son, as if caressing and angering him."}},{"n":30,"text":"तस्याश्वानातपत्रं च ध्वजं सूतमथो धनुः ।\nनिपात्य नकुलः संख्ये शङ्खं दध्मौ प्रतापवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Nakula, the mighty, felled his horses, umbrella, banner, charioteer and bow in battle, and blew his conch."}},{"n":31,"text":"धृष्टकेतुः कृपेनास्ताञ्छित्त्वा बहुविधाञ्शरान् ।\nकृपं विव्याध सप्तत्या लक्ष्म चास्याहरत्त्रिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Dhrishtaketu cut down the many arrows shot by Kripa and pierced Kripa with seventy, and took off his mark with three."}},{"n":32,"text":"तं कृपः शरवर्षेण महता समवाकिरत् ।\nनिवार्य च रणे विप्रो धृष्टकेतुमयोधयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Kripa covered him with a great shower of arrows, and warding him off in battle, the brahmin fought Dhrishtaketu."}},{"n":33,"text":"सात्यकिः कृतवर्माणं नाराचेन स्तनान्तरे ।\nविद्ध्वा विव्याध सप्तत्या पुनरन्यैः स्मयन्निव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Satyaki pierced Kritavarma between the breasts with a nârâcha arrow and again with seventy others, smiling as if at play."}},{"n":34,"text":"सप्तसप्ततिभिर्भोजस्तं विद्ध्वा निशितैः शरैः ।\nनाकम्पयत शैनेयं शीघ्रो वायुरिवाचलम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Bhoja pierced him with seventy-seven sharp arrows, but he did not shake the grandson of Shini, as a swift wind cannot shake a mountain."}},{"n":35,"text":"सेनापतिः सुशर्माणं शीघ्रं मर्मस्वताडयत् ।\nस चापि तं तोमरेण जत्रुदेशे अताडयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The commander quickly struck Sushrman in the vital places, and Sushrman struck him in the collarbone region with a javelin."}},{"n":36,"text":"वैकर्तनं तु समरे विराटः प्रत्यवारयत् ।\nसह मत्स्यैर्महावीर्यैस्तदद्भुतमिवाभवत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Virata with his mighty Matsyas held Karna, Vikartana's son, back in battle, and it was a marvel."}},{"n":37,"text":"तत्पौरुषमभूत्तत्र सूतपुत्रस्य दारुणम् ।\nयत्सैन्यं वारयामास शरैः संनतपर्वभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There was terrible prowess in the charioteer's son there, for he checked the army with arrows with bent joints."}},{"n":38,"text":"द्रुपदस्तु स्वयं राजा भगदत्तेन संगतः ।\nतयोर्युद्धं महाराज चित्ररूपमिवाभवत् ।\nभूतानां त्रासजननं चक्रातेऽस्त्रविशारदौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"King Drupada himself met Bhagadatta. Their battle, great king, was like a painting, and those two experts in weapons struck fear into beings."}},{"n":39,"text":"भूरिश्रवा रणे राजन्याज्ञसेनिं महारथम् ।\nमहता सायकौघेन छादयामास वीर्यवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhurishravas, the strong, covered the great chariot-warrior, Yajnasena's son Shikhandi, in battle with a great flood of arrows, O king."}},{"n":40,"text":"शिखण्डी तु ततः क्रुद्धः सौमदत्तिं विशां पते ।\nनवत्या सायकानां तु कम्पयामास भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"But Shikhandi, then enraged, shook Somadatta's son with ninety arrows, O lord of people, O Bharata."}},{"n":41,"text":"राक्षसौ भीमकर्माणौ हैडिम्बालम्बुसावुभौ ।\nचक्रातेऽत्यद्भुतं युद्धं परस्परवधैषिणौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"The two rakshasas of terrible deeds, Hidimba's son and Alambusa, fought an extremely wonderful battle, each wishing to kill the other."}},{"n":42,"text":"मायाशतसृजौ दृप्तौ मायाभिरितरेतरम् ।\nअन्तर्हितौ चेरतुस्तौ भृशं विस्मयकारिणौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Proud, creating hundreds of illusions, they roamed unseen in their own illusions against each other, causing great wonder."}},{"n":43,"text":"चेकितानोऽनुविन्देन युयुधे त्वतिभैरवम् ।\nयथा देवासुरे युद्धे बलशक्रौ महाबलौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Chekitana fought Anuvinda in a most fearful battle, like the mighty Bala and Shakra in the war of gods and asuras."}},{"n":44,"text":"लक्ष्मणः क्षत्रदेवेन विमर्दमकरोद्भृशम् ।\nयथा विष्णुः पुरा राजन्हिरण्याक्षेण संयुगे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Lakshmana fought Kshatradeva hard, as Vishnu once did against Hiranyaksha in battle, O king."}},{"n":45,"text":"ततः प्रजविताश्वेन विधिवत्कल्पितेन च ।\nरथेनाभ्यपतद्राजन्सौभद्रं पौरवो नदन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the Paurava, roaring, attacked Subhadra's son in a chariot with swift horses and fitted by rule, O king."}},{"n":46,"text":"ततोऽभियाय त्वरितो युद्धाकाङ्क्षी महाबलः ।\nतेन चक्रे महद्युद्धमभिमन्युररिंदमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Abhimanyu, destroyer of foes, mighty and eager for battle, came swiftly up and fought a great fight with him."}},{"n":47,"text":"पौरवस्त्वथ सौभद्रं शरव्रातैरवाकिरत् ।\nतस्यार्जुनिर्ध्वजं छत्रं धनुश्चोर्व्यामपातयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The Paurava covered Subhadra's son with floods of arrows, and Arjuna's son cut down his banner, umbrella and bow to the ground."}},{"n":48,"text":"सौभद्रः पौरवं त्वन्यैर्विद्ध्वा सप्तभिराशुगैः ।\nपञ्चभिस्तस्य विव्याध हयान्सूतं च सायकैः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Subhadra's son pierced the Paurava with seven other swift arrows, and with five he pierced his horses and charioteer."}},{"n":49,"text":"ततः संहर्षयन्सेनां सिंहवद्विनदन्मुहुः ।\nसमादत्तार्जुनिस्तूर्णं पौरवान्तकरं शरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, gladdening the army and roaring again and again like a lion, Arjuna's son quickly took up an arrow that would end the Paurava."}},{"n":50,"text":"द्वाभ्यां शराभ्यां हार्दिक्यश्चकर्त सशरं धनुः ।\nतदुत्सृज्य धनुश्छिन्नं सौभद्रः परवीरहा ।\nउद्बबर्ह सितं खड्गमाददानः शरावरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"With two arrows Hardikya's son cut his bow and its arrow, and discarding the cut bow, Subhadra's son, slayer of enemy heroes, took up a white sword and a shield."}},{"n":51,"text":"स तेनानेकतारेण चर्मणा कृतहस्तवत् ।\nभ्रान्तासिरचरन्मार्गान्दर्शयन्वीर्यमात्मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"With that shield of many stars, skilled, he moved with whirling sword along many paths, displaying his own valor."}},{"n":52,"text":"भ्रामितं पुनरुद्भ्रान्तमाधूतं पुनरुच्छ्रितम् ।\nचर्मनिस्त्रिंशयो राजन्निर्विशेषमदृश्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The whirled sword raised again, brandished and lifted once more, O king, was seen as no different from the shield and blade."}},{"n":53,"text":"स पौरवरथस्येषामाप्लुत्य सहसा नदन् ।\nपौरवं रथमास्थाय केशपक्षे परामृशत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Leaping suddenly with a shout onto the pole of the Paurava's chariot, then onto the chariot itself, he seized the Paurava by the hair."}},{"n":54,"text":"जघानास्य पदा सूतमसिनापातयद्ध्वजम् ।\nविक्षोभ्याम्भोनिधिं तार्क्ष्यस्तं नागमिव चाक्षिपत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He kicked his charioteer, felled his banner with the sword, and flung him as Tarkshya, having churned the ocean, hurls a snake."}},{"n":55,"text":"तमाकलितकेशान्तं ददृशुः सर्वपार्थिवाः ।\nउक्षाणमिव सिंहेन पात्यमानमचेतनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"All the kings saw him, hair gripped, senseless, like a bull being thrown down by a lion."}},{"n":56,"text":"तमार्जुनिवशं प्राप्तं कृष्यमाणमनाथवत् ।\nपौरवं पतितं दृष्ट्वा नामृष्यत जयद्रथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Seeing the Paurava fallen into the power of Arjuna's son and dragged like one without a protector, Jayadratha could not bear it."}},{"n":57,"text":"स बर्हिणमहावाजं किङ्किणीशतजालवत् ।\nचर्म चादाय खड्गं च नदन्पर्यपतद्रथात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking a shield and a sword, with a great peacock-feather ornament and net of a hundred little bells, he jumped roaring from his chariot."}},{"n":58,"text":"ततः सैन्धवमालोक्य कार्ष्णिरुत्सृज्य पौरवम् ।\nउत्पपात रथात्तूर्णं श्येनवन्निपपात च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Krishna's grandson, seeing the Saindhava, let go of the Paurava, leapt swiftly from the chariot and dropped like a hawk."}},{"n":59,"text":"प्रासपट्टिशनिस्त्रिंशाञ्शत्रुभिः संप्रवेरितान् ।\nचिच्छेदाथासिना कार्ष्णिश्चर्मणा संरुरोध च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Subhadra's son cut with the sword the spears, clubs and swords hurled by the enemies and blocked them with his shield."}},{"n":60,"text":"स दर्शयित्वा सैन्यानां स्वबाहुबलमात्मनः ।\nतमुद्यम्य महाखड्गं चर्म चाथ पुनर्बली ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having shown his own arm's strength to the armies, the mighty one again raised his great sword and shield,"}},{"n":61,"text":"वृद्धक्षत्रस्य दायादं पितुरत्यन्तवैरिणम् ।\nससाराभिमुखः शूरः शार्दूल इव कुञ्जरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"and advanced against the heir of Vriddhakshatra, his father's bitter enemy, like a tiger against an elephant, the hero."}},{"n":62,"text":"तौ परस्परमासाद्य खड्गदन्तनखायुधौ ।\nहृष्टवत्संप्रजह्राते व्याघ्रकेसरिणाविव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Meeting each other, with swords as teeth and claws, they struck each other gladly like a tiger and a lion."}},{"n":63,"text":"संपातेष्वभिपातेषु निपातेष्वसिचर्मणोः ।\nन तयोरन्तरं कश्चिद्ददर्श नरसिंहयोः ॥","meaning":{"en":"In the leaps, charges and falls of sword and shield, no one could see any difference between those two lions among men."}},{"n":64,"text":"अवक्षेपोऽसिनिर्ह्रादः शस्त्रान्तरनिदर्शनम् ।\nबाह्यान्तरनिपातश्च निर्विशेषमदृश्यत ॥","meaning":{"en":"The thrusts, the ring of the swords, the gaps between the weapons, and the blows outside and inside, appeared indistinguishable."}},{"n":65,"text":"बाह्यमाभ्यन्तरं चैव चरन्तौ मार्गमुत्तमम् ।\nददृशाते महात्मानौ सपक्षाविव पर्वतौ ॥","meaning":{"en":"Moving along the outer and inner course, the two great souls looked like two winged mountains."}},{"n":66,"text":"ततो विक्षिपतः खड्गं सौभद्रस्य यशस्विनः ।\nशरावरणपक्षान्ते प्रजहार जयद्रथः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then, as the glorious Subhadra's son whirled his sword, Jayadratha struck at the end of its shield-edge."}},{"n":67,"text":"रुक्मपक्षान्तरे सक्तस्तस्मिंश्चर्मणि भास्वरे ।\nसिन्धुराजबलोद्धूतः सोऽभज्यत महानसिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"The great sword stuck between the golden edges of that bright shield, and, shaken by the Sindhu king's force, it broke."}},{"n":68,"text":"भग्नमाज्ञाय निस्त्रिंशमवप्लुत्य पदानि षट् ।\nसोऽदृश्यत निमेषेण स्वरथं पुनरास्थितः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing the sword was broken, he leapt six steps, and in a blink was seen again on his own chariot."}},{"n":69,"text":"तं कार्ष्णिं समरान्मुक्तमास्थितं रथमुत्तमम् ।\nसहिताः सर्वराजानः परिवव्रुः समन्ततः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When Krishna's grandson, free from the battle, mounted a fine chariot, all the kings together surrounded him on every side."}},{"n":70,"text":"ततश्चर्म च खड्गं च समुत्क्षिप्य महाबलः ।\nननादार्जुनदायादः प्रेक्षमाणो जयद्रथम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the mighty heir of Arjuna, raising his shield and the stump of sword, roared, looking at Jayadratha."}},{"n":71,"text":"सिन्धुराजं परित्यज्य सौभद्रः परवीरहा ।\nतापयामास तत्सैन्यं भुवनं भास्करो यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Leaving the Sindhu king, Subhadra's son, destroyer of enemy heroes, scorched that army as the sun scorches the world."}},{"n":72,"text":"तस्य सर्वायसीं शक्तिं शल्यः कनकभूषणाम् ।\nचिक्षेप समरे घोरां दीप्तामग्निशिखामिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shalya hurled at him a terrible iron spear adorned with gold, like a blazing tongue of fire, in the battle."}},{"n":73,"text":"तामवप्लुत्य जग्राह सकोशं चाकरोदसिम् ।\nवैनतेयो यथा कार्ष्णिः पतन्तमुरगोत्तमम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Leaping, he caught it, and put his sword in its sheath, as Vinata's son might seize a falling great serpent."}},{"n":74,"text":"तस्य लाघवमाज्ञाय सत्त्वं चामिततेजसः ।\nसहिताः सर्वराजानः सिंहनादमथानदन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing his agility and the strength of that man of boundless energy, all the kings together gave a lion roar."}},{"n":75,"text":"ततस्तामेव शल्यस्य सौभद्रः परवीरहा ।\nमुमोच भुजवीर्येण वैडूर्यविकृताजिराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Subhadra's son, destroyer of enemy heroes, hurled that same spear at Shalya with the strength of his arm, its shaft set with beryl."}},{"n":76,"text":"सा तस्य रथमासाद्य निर्मुक्तभुजगोपमा ।\nजघान सूतं शल्यस्य रथाच्चैनमपातयत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Reaching his chariot like a snake let loose, it killed Shalya's charioteer and threw him from the chariot."}},{"n":77,"text":"ततो विराटद्रुपदौ धृष्टकेतुर्युधिष्ठिरः ।\nसात्यकिः केकया भीमो धृष्टद्युम्नशिखण्डिनौ ।\nयमौ च द्रौपदेयाश्च साधु साध्विति चुक्रुशुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Virata and Drupada, Dhrishtaketu, Yudhishthira, Satyaki, the Kekayas, Bhima, Dhrishtadyumna and Shikhandi, the twins and the sons of Draupadi cried out, \"Well done! Well done!\""}},{"n":78,"text":"बाणशब्दाश्च विविधाः सिंहनादाश्च पुष्कलाः ।\nप्रादुरासन्हर्षयन्तः सौभद्रमपलायिनम् ।\nतन्नामृष्यन्त पुत्रास्ते शत्रोर्विजयलक्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Various sounds of arrows and many lion roars arose, delighting Subhadra's son as he did not flee. Your sons could not bear that sign of the enemy's victory."}},{"n":79,"text":"अथैनं सहसा सर्वे समन्तान्निशितैः शरैः ।\nअभ्याकिरन्महाराज जलदा इव पर्वतम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all of them suddenly covered him from every side with sharp arrows, great king, as clouds do a mountain."}},{"n":80,"text":"तेषां च प्रियमन्विच्छन्सूतस्य च पराभवात् ।\nआर्तायनिरमित्रघ्नः क्रुद्धः सौभद्रमभ्ययात् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Wishing to please them and to avenge his charioteer's defeat, Shalya, son of Artayani, slayer of foes, in anger went against Subhadra's son."}}]}]}